title BUHR-J7r3 — a Brix descriptor declares artifacts the store satisfies
prompt Continue the agent-doable journey; land BUHR-J7r3 as its own signed round; send often; stop at custody gates
think Rungs one and two built the store and proved a manifest is an honest index. The exploration's third rung makes the Brix-facing half literal: a descriptor declares needed artifacts, evaluates to a manifest, and the store proves it satisfies the declaration.
think Modeled a Brix-facing format tablecloth-decl-v1 descriptor — one `require <name>` line per artifact a system needs. pond/apps/tablecloth_brix.rye evaluate joins the declaration with a live catalog: each required name contributes its true content address (tablecloth.address_hex + a new pub artifact_len), producing a format tablecloth-v1 manifest in declared order.
think The join refuses honestly: a required name the store cannot satisfy refuses the whole evaluation (Unsatisfied) rather than emitting a manifest naming bytes the store lacks; a bad header or an empty descriptor refuses BadDescriptor.
obs Closed the chain end to end: the evaluated manifest verifies against the live store by rung two (verify_against_store), so a system declares what it needs, the store proves it serves it, and the manifest is the audited receipt. Declared order is honored (site.md before notes.txt though stored the other way).
obs Caught a TAME ban before commit — used std.mem.copyForwards for the header, switched to tally_copy.copy_disjoint (the banned form, migrated on write). TAME bans clean, width clean, parseInt ratchet holds at 8.
obs Additive — rungs one and two stay their own GREEN binaries under the declaration layer; tablecloth.rye grew only a pub artifact_len.
obs Journey 7's agent-doable arc now stands: store (r1) · honest index (r2) · Brix declaration satisfied (r3). The remaining horizon rungs — owner-signed (Kumara-keyed) and Comlink-served — reach the custody/serve gates that are Keaton's hand.
loom witness=buhr_tablecloth_brix_witness declared=2 evaluated=2 verified=2 refusals=Unsatisfied/BadDescriptor
file pond/apps/tablecloth_brix.rye the declaration layer — evaluate a tablecloth-decl-v1 descriptor against a live store into a verified manifest
file pond/apps/tablecloth.rye additive: pub artifact_len (whole length by name)
file tools/buhr_tablecloth_brix_witness.rish the witness — declare·evaluate·verify, three refusals, r1 + r2 re-run
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md BUHR line appended with the J7r3 landing and the arc close; git nib
